From 7917b2886f0c0b4c1f125dae69b67353b8a35d47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: donghun <ehdgns1083@pusan.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:18:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fpga/vcu118: put the DDR4 calibration firmware into the
 bitstream

The DDR4 controller's calibration MicroBlaze boots from BRAM; this flow wrote
the bitstream with the IP's placeholder boot loop still in it, so the
controller never calibrated (seen on the board: LED 7 off, Vivado reports
empty MIG version registers). Nexus has the same step for its core
(vivado_hook_write_bitstream_post.tcl).

vcu118_ddr4_fw.tcl builds the MMI from the placed lmb_bram_I and
second_lmb_bram_I BRAMs (write_mem_info only describes the first bank, and
the ~86 KB firmware spans both), taking bank sizes from the BMM info and the
part from the design instead of Nexus's constants, and runs updatemem.
write_bitstream pre/post hooks run it in every build; it also runs
standalone on a routed checkpoint to fix an existing bitstream.
---
 fpga/BUILD                           |   3 +
 fpga/chip_vcu118.core                |   3 +
 fpga/vcu118_bitstream_post_hooks.tcl |  10 +++
 fpga/vcu118_bitstream_pre_hooks.tcl  |   9 +++
 fpga/vcu118_ddr4_fw.tcl              | 104 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 fpga/vcu118_setup_hooks.tcl          |   5 ++
 6 files changed, 134 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 fpga/vcu118_bitstream_post_hooks.tcl
 create mode 100644 fpga/vcu118_bitstream_pre_hooks.tcl
 create mode 100644 fpga/vcu118_ddr4_fw.tcl

